<% faqs << { question: "Should you lean back in powder?", answer: "Not much. A slightly more centered or back-of-center stance helps keep your tips up, but leaning far back tires your legs and reduces control." } %>
<% faqs << { question: "What skis are best for powder?", answer: "Wider skis with tip rocker float best in deep snow. Many rental shops offer wider demo skis on powder days." } %>
<% faqs << { question: "What is a tree well?", answer: "A pocket of deep, loose snow around the base of a tree. Falling in head-first can trap a skier, so stay away from tree trunks and ski with a partner on powder days." } %>
